 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Assignment 08 \u2014 Soil Health and Sustainability Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "**Objective:** Analyze soil health indicators and sustainability metrics for the 20 Maumee watershed fields.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key tasks:**\n",
    "1. Load and explore soil health data from SSURGO\n",
    "2. Calculate soil health indices (physical, chemical, biological indicators)\n",
    "3. Analyze relationships between soil properties and field management\n",
    "4. Assess sustainability metrics and environmental risk factors\n",
    "5. Create soil health visualization dashboards\n",
    "\n",
    "**Data sources:**\n",
    "- `data/fields/ohio_maumee_20.geojson` \u2014 20 field boundaries (EPSG:4326)\n",
    "- `data/soil/ohio_maumee_20_soil.csv` \u2014 SSURGO soil data\n",
    "- `data/ndvi/` \u2014 Sentinel-2 NDVI rasters (from previous assignments)\n",
    "- `data/weather/ohio_maumee_20_2020_2023.csv` \u2014 NASA POWER weather data\n",
    "- `data/cdl/ohio_maumee_20_cdl.csv` \u2014 Crop type classifications"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Setup and imports"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import geopandas as gpd\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "import os\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style='whitegrid', font_scale=1.1)\n",
    "\n",
    "DATA_DIR = Path('data')\n",
    "OUTPUT_DIR = Path('output')\n",
    "OUTPUT_DIR.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Setup complete.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Load field boundaries and soil data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load field boundaries and soil data\n",
    "fields_gdf = gpd.read_file(DATA_DIR / 'fields' / 'ohio_maumee_20.geojson')\n",
    "soil_df = pd.read_csv(DATA_DIR / 'soil' / 'ohio_maumee_20_soil.csv')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Loaded {len(fields_gdf)} field boundaries\")\n",
    "print(f\"Loaded {len(soil_df)} soil records\")\n",
    "print(f\"Soil columns: {list(soil_df.columns)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Explore soil health indicators"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "### Filter soil dataset for key indicators: OM, pH, and CEC\n",
    "\n",
    "CEC (Cation Exchange Capacity) is estimated using the formula: `CEC ≈ (clay% × 0.5) + (OM% × 2)`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Filter for key soil health indicators: Organic Matter, pH, and CEC\n",
    "# CEC estimation: CEC ≈ (clay% * 0.5) + (OM% * 2) - standard estimate for mineral soils\n",
    "soil_df['cec'] = (soil_df['clay_pct'] * 0.5) + (soil_df['om_pct'] * 2)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Select key indicators\n",
    "key_indicators = ['field_id', 'lat', 'lon', 'om_pct', 'ph', 'cec']\n",
    "soil_health = soil_df[key_indicators].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== Filtered Soil Health Indicators ===\")\n",
    "print(f\"Key indicators: Organic Matter (om_pct), pH, CEC (estimated)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Records: {len(soil_health)}\")\n",
    "print(\"\\n--- Summary Statistics ---\")\n",
    "display(soil_health[['om_pct', 'ph', 'cec']].describe())\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n--- Sample Data ---\")\n",
    "display(soil_health.head(10))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save filtered data\n",
    "output_path = DATA_DIR / 'soil' / 'ohio_maumee_20_soil_health.csv'\n",
    "soil_health.to_csv(output_path, index=False)\n",
    "print(f\"\\n✓ Saved filtered soil health data to: {output_path}\")"
   ]
  },
   {
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "metadata": {},
    "source": [
     "## 4. Calculate soil health indices"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "### Group by Field ID and calculate Soil Health Score\n",
    "\n",
    "The Soil Health Score is a composite of:\n",
    "- **Organic Matter Score (40%)**: Normalized to 0-100\n",
    "- **pH Score (30%)**: Optimal at 6.5, penalty for deviation\n",
    "- **CEC Score (30%)**: Normalized to 0-100 (nutrient holding capacity)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Normalize each indicator to 0-100 scale\n",
    "def normalize(series, min_val=None, max_val=None):\n",
    "    if min_val is None:\n",
    "        min_val = series.min()\n",
    "    if max_val is None:\n",
    "        max_val = series.max()\n",
    "    return ((series - min_val) / (max_val - min_val)) * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "# Score each indicator (higher is better for soil health)\n",
    "soil_health['om_score'] = normalize(soil_health['om_pct'])\n",
    "soil_health['ph_score'] = 100 - np.abs(soil_health['ph'] - 6.5) * 20\n",
    "soil_health['cec_score'] = normalize(soil_health['cec'])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate composite Soil Health Score (weighted average)\n",
    "soil_health['soil_health_score'] = (\n",
    "    soil_health['om_score'] * 0.4 +\n",
    "    soil_health['ph_score'] * 0.3 +\n",
    "    soil_health['cec_score'] * 0.3\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Sort by score (highest first)\n",
    "soil_health_ranked = soil_health.sort_values('soil_health_score', ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== Soil Health Score by Field ===\")\n",
    "print(\"(Score = 0-100, higher is better)\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"--- All Fields Ranked by Soil Health Score ---\")\n",
    "display(soil_health_ranked[['field_id', 'om_pct', 'ph', 'cec', 'soil_health_score']])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n--- Top 5 Fields (Highest Soil Health) ---\")\n",
    "display(soil_health_ranked.head())\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n--- Bottom 5 Fields (Lowest Soil Health) ---\")\n",
    "display(soil_health_ranked.tail())\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save ranked results\n",
    "output_path = DATA_DIR / 'soil' / 'ohio_maumee_20_soil_health_scores.csv'\n",
    "soil_health_ranked.to_csv(output_path, index=False)\n",
    "print(f\"\\n✓ Saved soil health scores to: {output_path}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Identify Fields with High Erosion Risk based on K-Factor\n",
    "\n",
    "K-Factor (Soil Erodibility) is calculated using:\n",
    "```\n",
    "K = (0.2 + 0.3×exp(-0.0256×sand)) × (1 - 0.25×OM/100) / (clay+silt)^0.3\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Combined erosion risk considers:\n",
    "- K-Factor (40%): Higher = more erodible soil\n",
    "- Low Infiltration (30%): Based on kSat - lower = higher risk\n",
    "- Low OM (30%): Lower organic matter = higher risk"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Calculate K-Factor (soil erodibility) estimate\n",
    "soil_df['k_factor'] = (\n",
    "    (0.2 + 0.3 * np.exp(-0.0256 * soil_df['sand_pct'])) * \n",
    "    (1 - 0.25 * soil_df['om_pct'] / 100) / \n",
    "    ((soil_df['clay_pct'] + soil_df['silt_pct']) ** 0.3)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Normalize components for risk scoring\n",
    "def normalize(series):\n",
    "    return (series - series.min()) / (series.max() - series.min())\n",
    "\n",
    "# Erosion risk score components\n",
    "soil_df['k_factor_risk'] = normalize(soil_df['k_factor']) * 100\n",
    "soil_df['low_infiltration_risk'] = (1 - normalize(soil_df['kSat'])) * 100\n",
    "soil_df['low_om_risk'] = (1 - normalize(soil_df['om_pct'])) * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "# Combined erosion risk score (higher = higher risk)\n",
    "soil_df['erosion_risk_score'] = (\n",
    "    soil_df['k_factor_risk'] * 0.4 +\n",
    "    soil_df['low_infiltration_risk'] * 0.3 +\n",
    "    soil_df['low_om_risk'] * 0.3\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Sort by erosion risk (highest first)\n",
    "erosion_ranked = soil_df.sort_values('erosion_risk_score', ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== Erosion Risk Assessment by Field ===\")\n",
    "print(\"(Higher score = higher erosion risk)\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"--- All Fields by Erosion Risk ---\")\n",
    "display(erosion_ranked[['field_id', 'k_factor', 'kSat', 'om_pct', 'erosion_risk_score']])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n--- High Erosion Risk Fields (>70) ---\")\n",
    "high_risk = erosion_ranked[erosion_ranked['erosion_risk_score'] > 70]\n",
    "display(high_risk)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n--- Low Erosion Risk Fields (<40) ---\")\n",
    "low_risk = erosion_ranked[erosion_ranked['erosion_risk_score'] < 40]\n",
    "display(low_risk)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save erosion risk data\n",
    "output_path = DATA_DIR / 'soil' / 'ohio_maumee_20_erosion_risk.csv'\n",
    "erosion_ranked.to_csv(output_path, index=False)\n",
    "print(f\"\\n✓ Saved erosion risk data to: {output_path}\")"
   ]
  },
   {
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "metadata": {},
    "source": [
     "## 5. Analyze relationships with NDVI and crop type"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "### Compare Organic Matter %: Top 10 vs Bottom 10 Productive Fields\n",
    "\n",
    "Productivity is ranked by NDVI (mean_ndvi from zonal statistics)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load zonal stats (NDVI) for productivity ranking\n",
    "zonal_df = pd.read_csv(OUTPUT_DIR / 'zonal_stats_rasterstats.csv')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Identify field ID column\n",
    "id_col = [c for c in zonal_df.columns if 'field_id' in c.lower()][0]\n",
    "zonal_df = zonal_df.rename(columns={id_col: 'field_id'})\n",
    "\n",
    "# Rank by NDVI (productivity proxy)\n",
    "zonal_df = zonal_df.sort_values('mean_ndvi', ascending=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Get top 10 and bottom 10\n",
    "top_10 = zonal_df.head(10)['field_id'].values\n",
    "bottom_10 = zonal_df.tail(10)['field_id'].values\n",
    "\n",
    "# Merge with soil data\n",
    "soil_with_prod = soil_df.merge(zonal_df[['field_id', 'mean_ndvi']], on='field_id', how='left')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add productivity category\n",
    "soil_with_prod['productivity'] = 'Unknown'\n",
    "soil_with_prod.loc[soil_with_prod['field_id'].isin(top_10), 'productivity'] = 'Top 10'\n",
    "soil_with_prod.loc[soil_with_prod['field_id'].isin(bottom_10), 'productivity'] = 'Bottom 10'\n",
    "\n",
    "# Filter to top/bottom\n",
    "plot_data = soil_with_prod[soil_with_prod['productivity'] != 'Unknown'].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Top 10 fields (highest NDVI): {list(top_10)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Bottom 10 fields (lowest NDVI): {list(bottom_10)}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create visualization\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Bar chart\n",
    "ax1 = axes[0]\n",
    "colors = {'Top 10': '#2ecc71', 'Bottom 10': '#e74c3c'}\n",
    "plot_sorted = plot_data.sort_values('mean_ndvi', ascending=False)\n",
    "bars = ax1.bar(range(len(plot_sorted)), plot_sorted['om_pct'], \n",
    "               color=[colors[p] for p in plot_sorted['productivity']], edgecolor='black')\n",
    "ax1.set_xticks(range(len(plot_sorted)))\n",
    "ax1.set_xticklabels([str(x)[-4:] for x in plot_sorted['field_id']], rotation=45, ha='right')\n",
    "ax1.set_xlabel('Field ID (last 4 digits)')\n",
    "ax1.set_ylabel('Organic Matter (%)')\n",
    "ax1.set_title('Organic Matter % by Field Productivity')\n",
    "ax1.legend(handles=[plt.Rectangle((0,0),1,1, color=c) for c in colors.values()], \n",
    "           labels=colors.keys(), loc='upper right')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Box plot\n",
    "ax2 = axes[1]\n",
    "sns.boxplot(data=plot_data, x='productivity', y='om_pct', hue='productivity', \n",
    "            palette=colors, ax=ax2, legend=False)\n",
    "ax2.set_xlabel('Productivity Category')\n",
    "ax2.set_ylabel('Organic Matter (%)')\n",
    "ax2.set_title('OM Distribution: Top 10 vs Bottom 10 Fields')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add mean annotations\n",
    "for i, cat in enumerate(['Bottom 10', 'Top 10']):\n",
    "    mean_val = plot_data[plot_data['productivity'] == cat]['om_pct'].mean()\n",
    "    ax2.annotate(f'Mean: {mean_val:.2f}%', xy=(i, mean_val), \n",
    "                ha='center', va='bottom', fontsize=10, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig(OUTPUT_DIR / '08_om_by_productivity.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== Summary Statistics ===\")\n",
    "display(plot_data.groupby('productivity')['om_pct'].describe())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Sustainability assessment"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": []
  },
   {
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "metadata": {},
    "source": [
     "## 7. Visualization dashboards"
    ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "### Spatial Plot: Soil Drainage Classes\n",
    "\n",
    "Drainage classes derived from kSat (saturated hydraulic conductivity) and clay content."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Derive drainage class from soil properties\n",
    "def classify_drainage(row):\n",
    "    kSat = row['kSat']\n",
    "    clay = row['clay_pct']\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if kSat > 25 and clay < 25:\n",
    "        return 'Well Drained'\n",
    "    elif kSat > 15 and clay < 30:\n",
    "        return 'Moderately Well Drained'\n",
    "    elif kSat > 8 and clay >= 25:\n",
    "        return 'Somewhat Poorly Drained'\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        return 'Poorly Drained'\n",
    "\n",
    "soil_df['drainage_class'] = soil_df.apply(classify_drainage, axis=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== Drainage Class Distribution ===\")\n",
    "display(soil_df['drainage_class'].value_counts())\n",
    "\n",
    "# Convert soil to GeoDataFrame and reproject\n",
    "soil_gdf = gpd.GeoDataFrame(\n",
    "    soil_df,\n",
    "    geometry=gpd.points_from_xy(soil_df['lon'], soil_df['lat']),\n",
    "    crs='EPSG:4326'\n",
    ").to_crs('EPSG:5070')\n",
    "\n",
    "fields_gdf_5070 = fields_gdf.to_crs('EPSG:5070')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Spatial join\n",
    "fields_with_drainage = gpd.sjoin_nearest(fields_gdf_5070, soil_gdf, how='left', distance_col='dist')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create spatial plot\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 1, figsize=(12, 10))\n",
    "\n",
    "drainage_colors = {\n",
    "    'Well Drained': '#2ecc71',\n",
    "    'Moderately Well Drained': '#3498db',\n",
    "    'Somewhat Poorly Drained': '#f39c12',\n",
    "    'Poorly Drained': '#e74c3c'\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot each drainage class\n",
    "for drainage_class, color in drainage_colors.items():\n",
    "    subset = fields_with_drainage[fields_with_drainage['drainage_class'] == drainage_class]\n",
    "    if len(subset) > 0:\n",
    "        subset.plot(ax=ax, color=color, edgecolor='black', linewidth=1.5, alpha=0.7)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create legend manually\n",
    "from matplotlib.patches import Patch\n",
    "legend_elements = [Patch(facecolor=color, edgecolor='black', label=f'{cls} ({len(fields_with_drainage[fields_with_drainage[\"drainage_class\"]==cls])})') \n",
    "                   for cls, color in drainage_colors.items()]\n",
    "ax.legend(handles=legend_elements, title='Drainage Class', loc='upper right', fontsize=10)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_title('Soil Drainage Classes - Ohio Maumee 20 Fields', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Easting (m)')\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('Northing (m)')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig(OUTPUT_DIR / '08_drainage_classes_spatial.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== Drainage Class Summary ===\")\n",
display(soil_df.groupby('drainage_class').agg({
    'kSat': 'mean',
    'clay_pct': 'mean',
    'awc': 'mean',
    'field_id': 'count'
}).rename(columns={'field_id': 'count'}))
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Final Dashboard: Soil Health & Sustainability"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Calculate all metrics for dashboard\n",
    "soil_df['cec'] = (soil_df['clay_pct'] * 0.5) + (soil_df['om_pct'] * 2)\n",
    "soil_df['k_factor'] = (\n",
    "    (0.2 + 0.3 * np.exp(-0.0256 * soil_df['sand_pct'])) * \n",
    "    (1 - 0.25 * soil_df['om_pct'] / 100) / \n",
    "    ((soil_df['clay_pct'] + soil_df['silt_pct']) ** 0.3)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "def normalize(series):\n",
    "    return (series - series.min()) / (series.max() - series.min())\n",
    "\n",
    "soil_df['om_score'] = normalize(soil_df['om_pct']) * 100\n",
    "soil_df['ph_score'] = 100 - np.abs(soil_df['ph'] - 6.5) * 20\n",
    "soil_df['cec_score'] = normalize(soil_df['cec']) * 100\n",
    "soil_df['soil_health_score'] = (\n",
    "    soil_df['om_score'] * 0.4 + soil_df['ph_score'] * 0.3 + soil_df['cec_score'] * 0.3\n",
    ")\n",
    "soil_df['k_factor_risk'] = normalize(soil_df['k_factor']) * 100\n",
    "soil_df['low_infiltration_risk'] = (1 - normalize(soil_df['kSat'])) * 100\n",
    "soil_df['low_om_risk'] = (1 - normalize(soil_df['om_pct'])) * 100\n",
    "soil_df['erosion_risk_score'] = (\n",
    "    soil_df['k_factor_risk'] * 0.4 + soil_df['low_infiltration_risk'] * 0.3 + soil_df['low_om_risk'] * 0.3\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "zonal_df = pd.read_csv(OUTPUT_DIR / 'zonal_stats_rasterstats.csv')\n",
    "id_col = [c for c in zonal_df.columns if 'field_id' in c.lower()][0]\n",
    "zonal_df = zonal_df.rename(columns={id_col: 'field_id'})\n",
    "merged = soil_df.merge(zonal_df[['field_id', 'mean_ndvi']], on='field_id')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Data prepared. Creating dashboard...\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create 4-panel dashboard\n",
    "fig = plt.figure(figsize=(16, 12))\n",
    "fig.suptitle('Soil Health & Sustainability Dashboard\\nOhio Maumee 20 Fields', \n",
    "             fontsize=18, fontweight='bold', y=0.98)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax1 = fig.add_subplot(2, 2, 1)\n",
    "scatter = ax1.scatter(merged['soil_health_score'], merged['erosion_risk_score'], \n",
    "                       c=merged['mean_ndvi'], cmap='RdYlGn', s=150, edgecolor='black', alpha=0.8)\n",
    "ax1.set_xlabel('Soil Health Score', fontsize=11)\n",
    "ax1.set_ylabel('Erosion Risk Score', fontsize=11)\n",
    "ax1.set_title('Soil Health vs Erosion Risk\\n(color = NDVI)', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "cbar = plt.colorbar(scatter, ax=ax1)\n",
    "cbar.set_label('NDVI (Productivity)', fontsize=10)\n",
    "ax1.axhline(y=50, color='gray', linestyle='--', alpha=0.5)\n",
    "ax1.axvline(x=50, color='gray', linestyle='--', alpha=0.5)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax2 = fig.add_subplot(2, 2, 2, projection='polar')\n",
    "categories = ['OM', 'pH', 'CEC', 'Low Erosion', 'Productivity']\n",
    "top5 = merged.nlargest(5, 'soil_health_score')\n",
    "angles = np.linspace(0, 2*np.pi, len(categories), endpoint=False).tolist()\n",
    "angles += angles[:1]\n",
    "colors = plt.cm.viridis(np.linspace(0, 0.8, 5))\n",
    "for idx, (_, row) in enumerate(top5.iterrows()):\n",
    "    values = [row['om_score'], row['ph_score'], row['cec_score'], \n",
    "              100 - row['erosion_risk_score'], row['mean_ndvi'] * 100]\n",
    "    values += values[:1]\n",
    "    ax2.plot(angles, values, 'o-', linewidth=2, label=str(row['field_id'])[-4:], color=colors[idx])\n",
    "ax2.set_xticks(angles[:-1])\n",
    "ax2.set_xticklabels(categories, fontsize=10)\n",
    "ax2.set_ylim(0, 100)\n",
    "ax2.legend(loc='upper right', bbox_to_anchor=(1.3, 1.0), fontsize=8, title='Field ID')\n",
    "ax2.set_title('Top 5 Fields - Multi-Indicator Profile', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold', pad=20)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax3 = fig.add_subplot(2, 2, 3)\n",
    "sustainability = merged.copy()\n",
    "sustainability['sustainability_cat'] = pd.cut(\n",
    "    sustainability['soil_health_score'], bins=[0, 40, 60, 80, 100], \n",
    "    labels=['Low', 'Moderate', 'Good', 'Excellent']\n",
    ")\n",
    "sustainability['erosion_cat'] = pd.cut(\n",
    "    sustainability['erosion_risk_score'], bins=[0, 30, 50, 70, 100],\n",
    "    labels=['Low', 'Moderate', 'High', 'Very High']\n",
    ")\n",
    "pivot = sustainability.groupby(['sustainability_cat', 'erosion_cat']).size().unstack(fill_value=0)\n",
    "pivot.plot(kind='bar', stacked=True, ax=ax3, colormap='RdYlGn_r', edgecolor='black')\n",
    "ax3.set_xlabel('Soil Health Category', fontsize=11)\n",
    "ax3.set_ylabel('Number of Fields', fontsize=11)\n",
    "ax3.set_title('Sustainability vs Erosion Risk', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax3.legend(title='Erosion Risk', fontsize=9)\n",
    "ax3.set_xticklabels(ax3.get_xticklabels(), rotation=0)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax4 = fig.add_subplot(2, 2, 4)\n",
    "soil_gdf = gpd.GeoDataFrame(soil_df, \n",
    "    geometry=gpd.points_from_xy(soil_df['lon'], soil_df['lat']), crs='EPSG:4326'\n",
    ").to_crs('EPSG:5070')\n",
    "fields_5070 = fields_gdf.to_crs('EPSG:5070')\n",
    "merged_gdf = gpd.sjoin_nearest(fields_5070, soil_gdf, how='left')\n",
    "merged_gdf.plot(column='soil_health_score', ax=ax4, cmap='RdYlGn', \n",
    "                edgecolor='black', linewidth=1.5, legend=True,\n",
    "                legend_kwds={'label': 'Soil Health Score', 'shrink': 0.6})\n",
    "ax4.set_title('Spatial Distribution: Soil Health Score', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax4.set_xlabel('Easting (m)')\n",
    "ax4.set_ylabel('Northing (m)')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(rect=[0, 0, 1, 0.96])\n",
    "plt.savefig(OUTPUT_DIR / '08_soil_health_dashboard.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== Dashboard Summary ===\")\n",
    "print(f\"Soil Health Score range: {merged['soil_health_score'].min():.1f} - {merged['soil_health_score'].max():.1f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Erosion Risk range: {merged['erosion_risk_score'].min():.1f} - {merged['erosion_risk_score'].max():.1f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"NDVI range: {merged['mean_ndvi'].min():.3f} - {merged['mean_ndvi'].max():.3f}\")"
   ]
